{"id":"646e9d56-64aa-4087-a5c4-43a212874d2b","object":"chat.completion","created":1785025743,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    segments = case['segments']\\n    budget = case['budget']\\n    n = len(segments)\\n    names = [s['name'] for s in segments]\\n    importance = [s['importance'] for s in segments]\\n    minimum = [s['minimum'] for s in segments]\\n    capacity = [s['capacity'] for s in segments]\\n    sum_min = sum(minimum)\\n    sum_cap = sum(capacity)\\n    if budget < sum_min or budget > sum_cap:\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\"Budget {budget} out of range [{sum_min}, {sum_cap}]\\\")\\n    allocations = list(minimum)\\n    remaining = budget - sum_min\\n    while remaining > 0:\\n        best_idx = None\\n        best_score = -1.0\\n        for i in range(n):\\n            if allocations[i] < capacity[i]:\\n                score = importance[i] / (allocations[i] + 1)\\n                if best_idx is None or score > best_score:\\n                    best_score = score\\n                    best_idx = i\\n        if best_idx is None:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"No segment can accommodate more tokens\\\")\\n        allocations[best_idx] += 1\\n        remaining -= 1\\n    by_name = {names[i]: allocations[i] for i in range(n)}\\n    total = sum(allocations)\\n    return {\\\"allocations\\\": allocations, \\\"by_name\\\": by_name, \\\"total\\\": total}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce a JSON response with key \"implementation\", containing Python source code for solve(case). The source must implement the described algorithm: allocate budget across segments, starting from each minimum, then greedily assign remaining budget to segment with highest importance divided by next allocated position (i.e., importance / (current_allocation+1)). Break ties by original segment order. Return dict with \"allocations\" (list of ints in segment order), \"by_name\" (dict mapping segment name to allocation), \"total\" (sum of allocations). Validate budget >= sum of minima and <= sum of capacities. Raise ValueError if not.\n\nThe output schema requires \"by_name\" to have dynamic keys from case.segments[*].name, so we must use the names exactly.\n\nWe'll write solve(case) that extracts segments list and budget. Compute sum_min, sum_cap, check. Initialize allocations array of length n with minima. Compute remaining budget. While remaining > 0, find best segment: for each segment i, if allocations[i] < capacity[i], compute score = importance[i] / (allocations[i] + 1). Pick max score, tie break by original index order. Increment allocation, decrement remaining.\n\nReturn dict with allocations, by_name (from names), total.\n\nWe'll include error handling. No mutation of case.\n\nNow produce JSON with implementation key. The Python source as a string, properly escaped.\n\nLet's write code and then format.\n\nCode:\n\n```\ndef solve(case):\n    segments = case['segments']\n    budget = case['budget']\n    n = len(segments)\n    # Extract properties\n    names = [s['name'] for s in segments]\n    importance = [s['importance'] for s in segments]\n    minimum = [s['minimum'] for s in segments]\n    capacity = [s['capacity'] for s in segments]\n    \n    sum_min = sum(minimum)\n    sum_cap = sum(capacity)\n    if budget < sum_min or budget > sum_cap:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Budget {budget} out of range [{sum_min}, {sum_cap}]\")\n    \n    allocations = list(minimum)  # copy\n    remaining = budget - sum_min\n    \n    while remaining > 0:\n        best_idx = None\n        best_score = -1.0\n        for i in range(n):\n            if allocations[i] < capacity[i]:\n                # Use integer division for comparison, but we need floating point? Use float division.\n                score = importance[i] / (allocations[i] + 1)\n                if best_idx is None or score > best_score:\n                    best_score = score\n                    best_idx = i\n                # tie: keep earlier index if equal, but we only update if score > best_score\n                # so earlier index is kept when equal. That's correct because we don't update on equal.\n        if best_idx is None:\n            # Should not happen because budget <= sum_cap\n            raise ValueError(\"No segment can accommodate more tokens\")\n        allocations[best_idx] += 1\n        remaining -= 1\n    \n    by_name = {names[i]: allocations[i] for i in range(n)}\n    total = sum(allocations)\n    return {\n        \"allocations\": allocations,\n        \"by_name\": by_name,\n        \"total\": total\n    }\n```\n\nMake sure to handle tie break correctly: we only update if score > best_score, so if equal we keep earlier index. That's fine.\n\nNow produce the JSON response.\n\nWe need to escape newlines, backslashes, quotes. We'll produce a single-line string. Use json.dumps in Python? But we are writing manually. We'll be careful.\n\nLet's produce the final answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1499,"completion_tokens":1124,"total_tokens":2623,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1408},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":779},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1408,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":91},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}